{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"e09625fd7f9370ce63d743bb4226775dcd09fa480c73b84053478fdafc47853d","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_9f624de65fa92f0861c4c913b846647f5fd359dc70a7ba0a53d151568c6ee715","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a novel Fast Chirplet Transform (FCT) and demonstrates its utility in accelerating and improving CNN-based audio classification. The methodological approach is sound, leveraging established scattering network principles and efficient convolution algorithms. Experimental results on bird and speech datasets support the claims of improved convergence and accuracy. However, the evaluation is limited by small dataset sizes, a lack of statistical significance testing, and the absence of comparisons against state-of-the-art deep learning baselines, which constrains the generalizability of the findings.","paper_id":"H1Fk2Iqex","paper_identity_sha256":"034e1f43b32936f80fa9bd81fc42a4989721fec2779696c6eed96f5a759c35b0","prompt_identity_sha256":"cb6cf7014f5feff1fae810a06c4d969b7fc872f85f55b95b30950edf073917b2","raw_response_sha256":"6b7f26bbe4435d54849e28564945c9f1033f2bb8bd82ee27e2d4e1f60eec72af","request_identity_sha256":"da94907dcd4fab86be6a72e406750652df28fd0d9d7c13e80ae6d0b4ddb3584a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"c19d61d08c61d0a7a677e36b5113d456e1856d4b5c07aac3cc60dd29ea83d34b","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-008","SRC-011","SRC-012"],"review_text":"The proposed Fast Chirplet Transform (FCT) is mathematically well-defined, extending the wavelet framework to include chirp rates. The authors correctly identify the infinite parameter space and impose a finite filter bank structure using parameters J and Q, consistent with standard time-frequency analysis. The algorithmic implementation leverages the scattering network framework (Bruna & Mallat, 2013) by applying a low-pass filter to the modulus of the convolution, which is a standard technique for introducing local time-invariance. The claim of reduced computational complexity from O(N log N) to O(N log M) via chunked convolution is technically valid and supported by the description of the implementation strategy. No conceptual errors or mis-specified objectives are apparent in the core methodological formulation.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-020","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The experimental design is limited by the scale of the datasets used. The bird classification experiment relies on the BIRD10 subset, which contains only 3 species and 15 minutes of recordings, making it difficult to assess the robustness of the method on larger, more diverse datasets. Similarly, the speech experiment uses a subset of TIMIT vowels (8 classes, 192 test utterances), which is a small sample size for statistical validation. While the paper compares FCT against raw audio and Mel features, it lacks comparisons against other state-of-the-art audio representations or deep learning architectures that might be more competitive. The authors acknowledge the limitation of the vowel experiment, stating it does not allow comparison with other papers, which is an honest assessment but highlights a gap in the experimental validation.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-017","SRC-019","SRC-025"],"review_text":"The paper provides sufficient detail for reproduction, including the specific hyperparameters for the FCT (J, Q, p, t, s) and the CNN architecture (layer sizes, activation functions, dropout rates, learning rate). The authors mention that the code is available and provide a URL for the BIRD10 dataset and features. The random seed is fixed for all experiments to ensure fair comparisons, which is a good practice. However, the paper does not provide a link to the code repository in the main text, only mentioning it in the acknowledgments and abstract. The detailed description of the CNN topology and training conditions (cross-entropy, L2 regularization) supports reproducibility, but the lack of a direct code link in the main body is a minor omission.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-016","SRC-018","SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper compares the proposed FCT-based CNN against baselines using raw audio and Mel spectrograms. These are standard and appropriate baselines for audio classification tasks. However, the paper does not compare against other recent or state-of-the-art methods for audio classification, such as other time-frequency representations or more advanced deep learning architectures. The authors acknowledge that the vowel experiment does not allow comparison with other papers, which suggests a lack of broader context in the literature. The comparison is limited to the specific datasets used, and there is no discussion of how the method performs relative to other approaches in the broader field of bioacoustic or speech recognition.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-019","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The paper reports results as single runs with fixed random seeds, which is a common practice in deep learning but does not provide statistical significance. There are no confidence intervals, error bars, or p-values reported for the improvements in MAP and accuracy. The reported gains (e.g., +7.8% MAP for birds, +2.3% accuracy for vowels) are presented as relative improvements, but without statistical testing, it is unclear whether these differences are significant or due to random variation. The small dataset sizes further limit the statistical power of the experiments. The authors do not discuss the variance in their results or the robustness of the improvements across different runs.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"3d613832a4e4d5ba12313fdfcad9cb53f7f3410ce6e6b569f2fed14a9c8ef315","paper_id":"H1Fk2Iqex","paper_ordinal":86,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"6b7f26bbe4435d54849e28564945c9f1033f2bb8bd82ee27e2d4e1f60eec72af","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1Fk2Iqex","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"01f149ced9e1e24d29af18556383babca535497d85f1892dcb9564559015fcd0","request_identity_sha256":"da94907dcd4fab86be6a72e406750652df28fd0d9d7c13e80ae6d0b4ddb3584a","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1215,"prompt_tokens":14265,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":15480},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"da94907dcd4fab86be6a72e406750652df28fd0d9d7c13e80ae6d0b4ddb3584a","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}